Theorem VF-5: end-to-end verification mandate — implementation + invariant enforcement + tests

  Preconditions:
    - VF-5 governs the end-to-end mandate per Annex E §AIMS VF-5: "Every
      active subsystem SHALL be end-to-end verified: implementation + invariant
      enforcement + tests. Missing any = incomplete." Restated by arc.md
      Non-Negotiable-Invariants #4: "The enabled surface must be end-to-end
      verified."
    - VF-5's concrete shape is Subsystem -> Bool per
      aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof. Discharged here
      against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry obligation.
    - This is a three-tier CONJUNCTION over each active subsystem: a subsystem
      is end-to-end verified IFF all three tiers (implementation AND invariant
      enforcement AND tests) are present. Dropping any one tier marks the
      subsystem incomplete.
    - TARGET-ONLY mandate: there is no single shipped verifier function — VF-5
      is a whole-subsystem completeness invariant the verification stack as a
      whole asserts (per arc.md Non-Negotiable-Invariants #4). conformance:
      target-only.

  Soundness property:
    Forall active subsystem S:

      (P1) Three-tier conjunction: S is end-to-end verified IFF S has an
           implementation AND S has invariant enforcement AND S has tests. The
           three tiers are independent and all mandatory.

      (P2) Any-missing = incomplete: if S is missing implementation, OR missing
           invariant enforcement, OR missing tests, then S is incomplete. The
           negative direction is exhaustive — there is no two-of-three partial
           credit.

    VF-5 is the completeness mandate: an active subsystem with code but no
    enforcement silently rots (the invariant degrades with no gate); one with
    enforcement but no tests has an unexercised gate; one with tests but no
    implementation is vacuous. All three are required for "active and verified".

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the structural_induction engine via three-tier
    composition over the subsystem (per the proof-checker design
    sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory VF row; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape — layered composition over the
    implementation / enforcement / tests tiers).

    Part (P1/P2) — three-tier conjunction grid:

      The verifier enumerates a (has_implementation, has_invariant_enforcement,
      has_tests) grid and asserts end-to-end-verified = the three-way AND:
        (impl, enforce, tests) -> complete
        (impl, enforce, no-tests) -> incomplete (missing tests)
        (impl, no-enforce, tests) -> incomplete (missing enforcement)
        (no-impl, enforce, tests) -> incomplete (missing implementation)
      Coverage gate: 4 subsystems (1 complete + 3 each-tier-missing).

    Negative-direction witness (the conjunction has teeth — a missing tier
    marks incomplete):
      A subsystem with implementation + tests but NO invariant enforcement is
      NOT marked complete; accepting it would let an unenforced invariant
      silently rot (the enforcement gate is absent, so the invariant degrades
      undetected).

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf5_end_to_end_mandate;
        three-tier conjunction over the subsystem grid; emits Fail on a
        complete/incomplete mismatch or a wrongly-accepted missing-tier
        subsystem)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest VF row)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      interprocedural_summary (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 structural_induction engine discharges VF-5 via the end-to-end three-tier conjunction (a subsystem is verified iff implementation AND invariant-enforcement AND tests): 1 complete subsystem + 3 each-tier-missing incomplete subsystems, with a negative-direction witness rejecting a subsystem that has implementation and tests but no invariant enforcement; VF-5 is a target-only whole-subsystem completeness mandate the verification stack asserts as a whole
